      <title>Commercial beekeeping: managing swarms and logistics</title>
      <link>https://www.farmersweekly.co.za/agri-business/agribusinesses/commercial-beekeeping-managing-swarms-and-logistics/#utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=commercial-beekeeping-managing-swarms-and-logistics</link>
      <description>Managing thousands of bee colonies as a pollination service provider is a complex, logistical feat. Added to the challenge is keeping the swarms fed amid dwindling natural resources and crops that offer little nutrition. Jaco Wolfaardt, commercial beekeeper and founder of Ubusi Beekeeping, spoke to Henning Naudé about keeping the bees and business abuzz.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.farmersweekly.co.za/agri-business/agribusinesses/commercial-beekeeping-managing-swarms-and-logistics/#utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=commercial-beekeeping-managing-swarms-and-logistics</guid>
